From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: controller startup retry
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

map-controller: bounded ieee1905 AL-MAC retry at startup (self-heal via procd)

At startup mapcontroller resolves its AL-MAC via cntlr_get_ieee1905_almac() ->
ubus_invoke(ieee1905, "info", ..., 2000ms). If ieee1905d is momentarily slow
enumerating interfaces at boot the reply can time out, or the AL-MAC can be zero
before the AL bridge is up.

The original code returned that error to run_controller(), which did `goto
out_exit` -> the process exits and procd respawns it -> it succeeds on a later
attempt once ieee1905d is responsive. That exit-and-respawn is the self-heal.

Ride out a bounded window (~20 x 1s) of transient ieee1905d slowness instead of
exiting on the very first timeout, but on exhaustion RETURN THE ERROR so
run_controller() takes `goto out_exit` and procd respawns us. Never loop forever
in-process on a wedged ieee1905d - that would remove the self-heal entirely and
make a wedge unrecoverable. Combined with `respawn 3600 5 0` (retry=0 = respawn
forever) in the init.d this gives both self-heal and never-permanently-dead.
--- a/src/cntlr_ubus.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_ubus.c
@@ -1744,18 +1744,35 @@
 
 int cntlr_get_ieee1905_almac(struct controller *c, uint8_t *almacaddr)
 {
+	static const uint8_t zero[6] = {0};
 	uint32_t obj;
-	int ret;
+	int ret = -1, tries;
 
 	if (!almacaddr)
 		return -1;
 
-	memset(almacaddr, 0, 6);
-	ret = cntlr_wait_for_object_timeout(c, "ieee1905", -1, &obj);
-	if (!ret)
-		ret = ubus_call_object(c, obj, "info", ieee1905_cb_get_almac, almacaddr);
-
-	return ret;
+	/* Ride out transient ieee1905d slowness at boot: the 'info' reply can
+	 * time out while ieee1905d is enumerating, and the AL-MAC can be zero
+	 * before the AL bridge is up. Retry with a 1s backoff, but BOUNDED - on
+	 * exhaustion return the error so run_controller() takes 'goto out_exit'
+	 * and procd respawns us (respawn-forever). Never wait forever in-process
+	 * on a wedged ieee1905d - that removed the exit-and-respawn self-heal. */
+	for (tries = 0; tries < 20; tries++) {
+		memset(almacaddr, 0, 6);
+
+		ret = cntlr_wait_for_object_timeout(c, "ieee1905", -1, &obj);
+		if (!ret)
+			ret = ubus_call_object(c, obj, "info", ieee1905_cb_get_almac, almacaddr);
+
+		if (!ret && memcmp(almacaddr, zero, 6) != 0)
+			return 0;
+
+		warn("cntlr: waiting for ieee1905 AL-MAC (try %d/20)...\n", tries + 1);
+		sleep(1);
+	}
+
+	err("cntlr: ieee1905 AL-MAC not ready; exiting for procd respawn\n");
+	return ret ? ret : -1;
 }
 
 static uint16_t ieee1905_media_str_to_type(const char *media)
